@page "/about"
<PageTitle>Architecture and Tech Stack - Free Library</PageTitle>

<h1 class="firstHeading">Architecture and Tech Stack</h1>

<p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:1.5em;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.6;">
    Free Library is built with modern, high-performance web engineering standards.
    The entire digital catalogue is loaded once into browser memory for instantaneous client-side navigation,
    backed by serverless edge functions and distributed cloud storage.
</p>

<h2 class="section-title">System Architecture</h2>

<div class="tech-grid">
    <div class="tech-card">
        <div class="tech-card-header">
            <span class="tech-card-title">Frontend Framework</span>
            <span class="tech-card-tag">Blazor WASM</span>
        </div>
        <p class="tech-card-desc">
            Single Page Application built with ASP.NET Core Blazor WebAssembly on .NET 10.
            Executes entirely client-side in the browser on a WebAssembly virtual machine.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tech-card">
        <div class="tech-card-header">
            <span class="tech-card-title">Core Language</span>
            <span class="tech-card-tag">C# 13</span>
        </div>
        <p class="tech-card-desc">
            Type-safe, modern C# 13 for all application logic, routing, component state management,
            and custom data structures with zero JavaScript framework dependencies.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tech-card">
        <div class="tech-card-header">
            <span class="tech-card-title">Search & DSA Engine</span>
            <span class="tech-card-tag">Algorithms</span>
        </div>
        <p class="tech-card-desc">
            In-memory Inverted Index for fast multi-token candidate intersection, Prefix Trie for real-time
            keystroke search, bounded LRU query cache, and O(1) letter hash buckets.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tech-card">
        <div class="tech-card-header">
            <span class="tech-card-title">Serverless API</span>
            <span class="tech-card-tag">Node.js 22</span>
        </div>
        <p class="tech-card-desc">
            Lightweight Vercel Serverless Functions written in modern JavaScript (ESM).
            Handles rate limiting, download analytics, and instant 302 edge redirects in under 20 milliseconds.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tech-card">
        <div class="tech-card-header">
            <span class="tech-card-title">Storage & CDN</span>
            <span class="tech-card-tag">Vercel Blob</span>
        </div>
        <p class="tech-card-desc">
            PDF files are stored in a public Vercel Blob store and distributed across Vercel's global Anycast Edge Network,
            serving downloads directly from edge caches at line rate.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tech-card">
        <div class="tech-card-header">
            <span class="tech-card-title">Database & Cache</span>
            <span class="tech-card-tag">Upstash Redis</span>
        </div>
        <p class="tech-card-desc">
            Serverless in-memory Redis KV database providing atomic sliding-window IP rate limiting
            (25 requests per 2-minute window) and live download statistics.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<h2 class="section-title">Technical Specifications</h2>

<table class="tech-table">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Layer</th>
            <th>Technology</th>
            <th>Implementation Details</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Client Runtime</strong></td>
            <td><code>WebAssembly (WASM)</code></td>
            <td>Near-native bytecode execution in browser with AOT compilation and assembly trimming</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Frontend</strong></td>
            <td><code>Blazor .NET 10</code></td>
            <td>Razor component model, C# 13, zero third-party CSS or JS frameworks</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Design System</strong></td>
            <td><code>Vanilla CSS</code></td>
            <td>Engineering-grade CSS variables, dark and light modes, zero-FOUC localStorage persistence</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Search Engine</strong></td>
            <td><code>In-Memory DSA</code></td>
            <td>Inverted Index token sets, Prefix Trie, bounded LRU query cache (64 slots)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Edge API</strong></td>
            <td><code>Vercel Functions</code></td>
            <td>ESM handlers on Node.js 22 runtime: /api/download and /api/stats</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Edge Cache</strong></td>
            <td><code>Anycast CDN</code></td>
            <td>HTTP 302 caching (s-maxage=604800) and worldwide Anycast Blob caching</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Distributed KV</strong></td>
            <td><code>Upstash Redis</code></td>
            <td>Serverless Redis REST API for sliding rate limiter and download counters</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>CLI & Automation</strong></td>
            <td><code>C# LibraryTool</code></td>
            <td>Custom CLI tool for PDF catalog generation, Vercel Blob synchronization, and CI/CD</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 class="section-title">Privacy and Security Measures</h2>

<p class="muted" style="line-height:1.6;">
    Free Library requires <strong>no accounts, no cookies, no logins, and no advertising trackers</strong>.
    The only dynamic server processing is an anonymous download counter and an automated sliding-window rate limiter
    to protect network bandwidth against automated scrapers.
</p>
